        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "West is the easternmost municipality in Holmes County and serves as a key gateway to the Big Black River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "West borders the Big Black River to the east, which also marks the Attala County line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1989, West made national news when East Holmes Academy refused to play a football game against Heritage Academy because Heritage had a black player.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Route 51 passes through West, connecting it to Vaiden and Durant and providing a vital link for local commuters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
